{pad:ignore}
<p><code>{section:hero}</code> puts a block of a landing page on the page - a hero, the features, the prices,
what customers say, the questions, a call to action, the numbers, the steps, the team, the logos,
a newsletter form, the contact details, a gallery or the footer. Every section is a file of
<code>pad/subs/sections/types/</code>, its style in <code>www/assets/sections/</code>; the files of
<code>types/</code> are the sections there are. It is HTML and CSS only - the questions open and close
by themselves, the forms post back without a script.</p>

<p>The section is selected by its prefix and name: <code>{section:hero title='...'}</code>. The heading is its first parameter, or <code>title=</code>.</p>

<p>Its parts come three ways, the first that has one winning: a <code>{pad:slot 'name'}</code> pair
directly in its content, an option of the part's name, and - for the text under the heading - the
rest of the content. A slot is template: it renders where the section stands, a field of the loop
around it, a tag. A section that lists things - features, plans, quotes, questions, numbers,
steps, people, logos, pictures, the footer's columns - takes its items from the rows of
<code>data=</code>, by their fields, and from <code>{section:item}</code> pairs inside it: the item's
first value is its name, its options its fields, its content its text - a plan's features a
line each, a question's answer.</p>

<p>The newsletter and the contact form post back to the page as <code>{input:form}</code> does - the
session's token and the form's name, so the page's PHP asks <code>padPosted ( 'newsletter' )</code>
and checks the post with <code>padValidate</code>; the fields refill and show the messages, and once
the post came back right the section says thanks in the form's place.</p>

<p>Each section is a size container: its layout follows the room it has, not the window. The colours
are <code>--pad-section-bg</code>, <code>-panel</code>, <code>-text</code>, <code>-soft</code>,
<code>-dim</code>, <code>-line</code>, <code>-accent</code>, <code>-accent-text</code> and
<code>-accent-soft</code>, falling back to the frame's palette, so a theme colours them;
<code>--pad-section-hero</code>, <code>-radius</code>, <code>-max</code>, <code>-font</code> and
<code>-heading-font</code> the rest. The style is written once per page with the CSP nonce.</p>
{/pad:ignore}
